{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183897-do-non-angelic-creatures-produce-aether-when-they-burn-essence","id":183897,"title":"Do non-angelic creatures produce Aether when they burn Essence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-29T11:34:31-07:00","id":183897,"title":"Do non-angelic creatures produce Aether when they burn Essence?","content":"I'm going to be running a Demon/Werewolf crossover game when IC comes out, and I realize it will be extremely important to determine if spirits, and especially if werewolves, give off Aether when they use Essence. I'm inclined to say no either way for the purposes of this game, but it got me to wondering how it works by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T11:46:49-07:00","id":183919,"title":"","content":"I remember one of the devs talking about this, so I an reliably say...no.<br /> <br /> Each supernatural that processes Essence puts a different kind of output-like if different kinds of engines produced different kinds of smoke and what have you from gasoline. THe God-Machine's waste is Aether, a Werewolf's waste is something else entirely.<br /> <br /> That said, if it makes the story interesting, go for it, but as is it requires the God-Machine's lot to turn Essence into Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T12:05:56-07:00","id":183946,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, and is how I was planning to run it in this particular game anyway. Don't want the werewolf players acting as walking batteries for the demon players. Thanks for the concise and thorough answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:01:26-07:00","id":183979,"title":"","content":"That said, some enterprising Inquisitor is going to say &quot;Well, surely there's no harm in <i>trying</i>, right guys?&quot;<br /> <br /> At which point you have all the excuse you need for a session's worth of weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:14:15-07:00","id":183987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183897-do-non-angelic-creatures-produce-aether-when-they-burn-essence?p=183979#post183979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, some enterprising Inquisitor is going to say &amp;quot;Well, surely there's no harm in <i>trying</i>, right guys?&amp;quot; At which point you have all the excuse you need for a session's worth of weirdness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, no doubt. Made all the weirder by the fact that I'm messing with the setting assumptions a lot to make more of a connection between Demon and Werewolf. When demons can siphon Aether from Loci and werewolves can step sideways at occult matrices, the players are bound to try all kinds of experiments to find out how spirits and the God Machine are connected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:56:27-07:00","id":184522,"title":"","content":"An exception maybe a spirit with essence eater though.<br /> <br /> An ephemeral with essence eater is able to consume other types of essence to replenish their own pool.<br /> <br /> Whenever god-machine essence is used up it produces aether, so wouldn't god-machine essence being converted into spirit essence produce aether?<br /> <br /> If you see essence eater is instead just allowing the ephemeral to consume and use all types of essence, then logically the spirit ought to be able to produce aether when it uses any god-machine essence it might have gotten its hands on. <br /> <br /> It's not really a new source of aether, but if the werewolves can make a deal with spirits with essence eater the demons might have another way to get aether out of the god-machine and its minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:55:26-07:00","id":184555,"title":"","content":"...Maybe. Essence doesn't quite work that way, but I can see a nitch.<br /> <br /> Essence, putting it simply, is an extremely fundamental energy/substance in the world, as near a universal power source as it gets-even Fuels like Glamour and Plasm might have ties to it. THAT SAID, each monster handles it differently, like a different catalyst for the same chemical. The mixture of Essence+Monster Metaphysics=Resultant Effect of Use+Waste. It's the same starting material, but once processed it becomes something else. Essence stored hasn't been properly catalyzed yet- it's like gasoline sitting in your tank. At least, that's how discussion has gone so far.<br /> <br /> The other catch arises from the results. Let's assume that each creature handles Essence kind of like our own digestive tracks, and that Essence goes through various stages of being broken down while being digested before it's used, a preparatory state, Essence tinged with the creature. The problem that emerges from that is that such essence is still mixing with the catalysts of the Essence Eater, so the result is a wholly new product once used-in this case, Pre-Aether Essence mixed in with the transformative elements of the Spirit. It's like ABC Gum, but with the fundamental building block of the world and more confusing results. But in this model, It might resemble Aether, but it'll also resemble whatever Spirits shit out.<br /> <br /> All of this is assuming Spirits produce waste. Ghosts might, and Angels definitely do, but even Magath strike me as surprisingly efficient clean machines for metaphysical fuels, since they just incorporate the new essence into their identity and proceed to poop out the new Essence as they grow from eating it.<br /> <br /> And ALL OF THIS is assuming the supernatural even closely resembles the scientific models of life as we know it, which, as I keep telling the Null Mysteriis, is pure bullshit, so ignore all of that and do what seems like the most fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:18:00-07:00","id":193158,"title":"","content":"My thinking has always been this: Essence is not Aether. It's Essence. It is the pure power of the universe, the base compound of magic or at least pretty close to it. When a living being, like a mouse or a man move around they might passively absorb the Essence around them. This might explain the power of Vitae. Sekhem might be the product of Essence being processed by the sacred geometric laws of ancient Irem. Mana might be what happens when a mage utilizes Essence in their will-working. So, in the end, Essence isn't Aether. Aether is what Essence becomes when an angel or a piece of infrastructure or perhaps a cryptid have the Essence travel through their complex metaphysics and come out changed. For many magical beings, the final product, the changed essence might be what they then use as their metaphysical fuel. For the God-Machine it is the process of transforming Essence into Aether that is important to it, not the Aether product itself and so it is discarded. Demons then are able to tap into this waste product. (I may have just said what ArcaneArts just said though. &gt;.&gt;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T23:41:36-07:00","id":193217,"title":"","content":"You did, but it never hurts to restate things-some people say it better for certain audiences.<br /> <br /> Although Mana is one of hte rare fuels types that really probably doesn't have anything to do with Essence-it and Pyros and <i>maybe</i> Pillars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:04:41-07:00","id":193375,"title":"","content":"I agree, I don't think Pyros is the same as Qashmallim - while superficially similar to angels - seem to follow different laws. As for Mana, I've never actually played mage, so I defer to greater wisdom on that topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:22:34-07:00","id":193546,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about house ruling it to allow this, but with some cool, weird, concomitant consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}